2026-09-21T07:04:03.4126023Z       "body": "## Pull Request\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nPlease start with a GitHub Discussion.\r\n\r\nOnce a team member asks you to open a PR, create it and link the discussion here.\r\n\r\nTypos, grammar issues, broken links and other small docs improvements should be reported in the pinned Discussion thread \"✏️ Report small docs improvements, including typos or broken links\".\r\nPlease do not open a PR for these yourself.\r\n-->\r\n\r\nDiscussion: https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/discussions/16382\r\n\r\n## Description\r\n\r\nWhen specifying an explicit `response_model` (such as `response_model=Item`, `response_model=Iterator[Item]`, or `response_model=AsyncIterable[Item]`) on generator streaming endpoints (JSONL and SSE), it was ignored during response serialization and generated an empty OpenAPI `itemSchema: {}`.\r\n\r\n### Root Cause\r\nIn `_populate_api_route_state()`, `get_stream_item_type()` was only called when `response_model` was an instance of `DefaultPlaceholder`. When an explicit `response_model` was provided:\r\n1. `route.stream_item_type` was never populated, leaving `stream_item_field` as `None`.\r\n2. `route.response_field` was erroneously populated instead.\r\n3. At runtime, streaming endpoints serialize items via `stream_item_field`. Because it was `None`, serialization fell back to `jsonable_encoder()`, bypassing model validation and field filters (`response_model_include`, `response_model_exclude`, `response_model_exclude_none`).\r\n4. OpenAPI generation emitted an empty `itemSchema: {}` because `stream_item_field` was absent.\r\n\r\n### Fix\r\nIn `_populate_api_route_state()`:\r\n- Check if the route is a streaming generator (`is_sse_stream` or `is_json_stream`) with an explicit `response_model`.\r\n- Extract the item model using `get_stream_item_type(response_model) or response_model`.\r\n- If it is not `ServerSentEvent`, assign `route.stream_item_type = stream_item`.\r\n- Set `response_model = None` so `stream_item_field` is created for per-item serialization, validation, and OpenAPI generation.\r\n\r\n### Tests Added\r\nAdded `tests/test_stream_response_model.py` covering:\r\n- Async JSONL stream with explicit model and field filtering (`response_model_exclude`, `response_model_exclude_none`)\r\n- Async JSONL stream with `response_model=AsyncIterable[Item]`\r\n- Sync generator JSONL stream with `response_model=Iterator[Item]`\r\n- SSE stream with explicit model and field exclusion\r\n- SSE stream yielding `ServerSentEvent` directly\r\n- SSE stream with explicit `response_model=ServerSentEvent`\r\n- Non-streaming endpoints unaffected\r\n- Validation error raised on invalid yielded chunk in async stream\r\n- Validation error raised on invalid yielded chunk in sync stream\r\n- Router inclusion via `app.include_router()`\r\n- OpenAPI schema generation (`itemSchema` for JSONL and `contentSchema` for SSE)\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] This PR links to a GitHub Discussion for the proposed code change.\r\n- [x] I added tests for the change.\r\n- [x] The new or updated tests fail on the main branch and pass on this PR.\r\n- [x] Coverage stays at 100%.\r\n- [x] The documentation explains the change if needed.",
